    "result": "Perfect! The fix is working correctly. The workflow file was created with the proper content.\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:** When passing `--ci` through the `frai` CLI to `frai-gate`, the flag was being lost because the action handler for the `gate` command was only forwarding the variadic `args` array, which didn't include unknown options like `--ci`.\n\n**The Solution:** Changed the gate command handler in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to extract all arguments directly from `process.argv` after the `gate` subcommand, preserving the original command-line arguments including flags. This ensures that all options passed to `frai gate` are properly forwarded to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\nThe fix:\n- Captures everything after 'gate' from `process.argv` to preserve the full argument list\n- Passes these arguments directly to `spawnSync` when delegating to `frai-gate`\n- Rebuilt with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested successfully - both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created",
